  "name": "Don Cossack song (village polyphony of the Don)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The song tradition of the Cossack stanitsas along the Don, whose old capital was Starocherkassk, with historical, military and drawn-out lyrical songs sung by groups of men and women. Its polyphony sets a high solo upper voice, the dishkant, above the leading line and a body of lower voices. Aleksandr Listopadov collected the repertoire with the phonograph and in the field for his Pesni donskikh kazakov, and the emigre Don Cossack Choir of Serge Jaroff carried an arranged choral form abroad.",
  "recipe": "classic modern don cossack song, ballad Poetry, Slavic bard branch. choral. heterophonic same melody variant ornament per voice global traditional polyphonic choir ensemble. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
